course: dictionary
lesson: 15553
title: Watching over
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Supervising means watching over people or an activity to make sure it is done safely and correctly. Look at this: «Mrs Patel is supervising the children while they swim.» Who is watching? Mrs Patel. What is she watching for? Safety, so the children swim safely.
explain: Supervising can also be an adjective, which describes a noun. «The supervising teacher checked the science experiment before it started.» The supervising teacher is the adult in charge. Put "in charge" in its place and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Without supervision» means no adult is watching. The clues are "without" and "supervision", so you know that nobody is keeping an eye on things. Ask yourself what would be missing: someone to watch over the children.
fact: Supervising means watching over people or an activity to make sure it is done safely and correctly.
fact: «Adult supervision» means a grown-up is watching over children.
fact: «Supervising the children» means keeping an eye on them.
fact: As an adjective, supervising means in charge: «the supervising teacher».
fact: «On playground duty» means a teacher is supervising the playground.
exercise: «Mrs Patel is supervising the children while they swim.» What is Mrs Patel doing? | *Watching over the children to keep them safe | Cooking lunch for the class | Cleaning the pool | Swimming faster than them
exercise: «The supervising teacher checked the science experiment before it started.» What does supervising mean here? | Painting the classroom walls | Sleeping in the corner | *In charge | Singing loudly
exercise: Which activity needs a supervising adult? | Reading a comic in bed | Drawing a picture alone at a desk | *Cooking with a hot stove
test: At lunchtime, Mr Lee is on playground duty. What does this mean? | Mr Lee is playing football | Mr Lee is cooking lunch | Mr Lee has gone home | *Mr Lee is supervising the children outside
test: «Without supervision» means what? | Doing homework with a friend | *No adult is watching | Everyone is watching the adult | A new bike
exam: Which phrase means a grown-up is watching over children to keep them safe? | *Adult supervision | Empty classroom | Loud music | Pencil case
